      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "19"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "List them all",
        "body": "Digit sum $4$:\n\n- one digit: $4$\n- two digits: $13, 22, 31, 40$\n- three digits: $103, 112, 121, 130, 202, 211, 220, 301, 310, 400$\n\n($1000$ has digit sum $1$.) That is $15$ numbers. The even ones and multiples of $10$ are not prime; $121 = 11^2$ and $301 = 7 \\times 43$ are not prime. The primes are $13, 31, 103, 211$: four of them.\n\nThe fraction is $\\frac{4}{15}$, so $a + b = 19$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 19**"
      }
    ],
