    "points": 8,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Raymonde's financial institution publishes a list of service charges as shown in the table. For her first twenty five transactions, she uses Autodebit three times as often as she writes cheques. She also writes as many cheques as she makes cash withdrawals. After her twenty-fifth transaction, she begins to make single transactions. What is the smallest number of transactions she needs to make so that her monthly service charges will exceed the \\$15.95 'all-in-one' fee?",
    "image": "qimages/cemc/gauss8-1999/q24.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "29"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "30"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "27"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "28"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "31"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Groups of five",
        "body": "In her first $25$ transactions the ratio cheque : cash : autodebit is $1 : 1 : 3$, so they come in groups of $5$ costing $0.50 + 0.45 + 3 \\times 0.60 = 2.75$ dollars. Five groups cost $5 \\times 2.75 = 13.75$ dollars.\n\nTo exceed \\$15.95 she needs more than \\$2.20 more. Using the most expensive item (Autodebit, \\$0.60) to need as few as possible: $3$ give \\$1.80 (not enough) and $4$ give \\$2.40 (enough). So the total is $25 + 4 = 29$ transactions.\n\n**Answer: (A) 29**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
