      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find the slant height",
        "body": "In the pyramid, the apex is $4$ cm above the centre of the base, and the centre is $3$ cm from the midpoint of each base edge. The height of each triangle (from the midpoint of its base edge to the apex) is therefore $\\sqrt{4^2 + 3^2} = 5$ cm.\n\nEach triangle has area $\\frac12 \\times 6 \\times 5 = 15\\text{ cm}^2$, four of them $60\\text{ cm}^2$, plus the square $36\\text{ cm}^2$: total $96\\text{ cm}^2$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $96\\text{ cm}^2$**"
      }
